  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Response to Support Flood-Affected Populations in Nigeria and Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria has been in the grip of the worst flood crisis in the last decade. The destructive flooding has affected more than 3.2 million people and caused massive damage to people&apos;s homes and community infrastructure. The floods destroyed farmlands, shelters, water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) infrastructures, sources of livelihood, and caused further displacement of populations. The project is targeting flood-affected populations, including displaced populations, returnees and host communities. Activities are being implemented in displacement sites as well as host communities, with direct assistance in the form of shelter repair kits, non-food items (NFI), WASH services, site facilitation and cash and voucher assistance. In 2022, Chad has faced the worst flooding since 1961. Between July and August 2022, flooding from excessive rainfall led to over 440,000 individuals being affected across the country. IOM through this project will distribute emergency shelter kits and NFI kits in the Lac Province and multipurpose cash-based interventions in N&apos;Djamena.</narrative>
  </description>
